item.description:
• [EE] Make the :autoOrient formatter more robust when DOCX files are edited with Microsoft Word Online.<br/>• [EE] The :html formatter now renders the <sup> , <sub> , <mark> , <code> , <kbd> , <samp> , and <pre> elements in ODT/DOCX/PDF documents. This is a pre-release feature: it requires {o.preReleaseFeatureIn=5011000} in the template, otherwise the content of these tags is rendered without formatting. <sup> / <sub> : renders text as superscript / subscript. <mark> : applies a fixed yellow highlight (color not customizable). <code> / <kbd> / <samp> â applies the Courier New font. <pre> : renders preformatted text, preserving newline characters (
, 
), with the Courier New font. An empty paragraph is added after the block to mimic the browser's bottom spacing. Options affecting <pre> : nospace : removes the empty paragraph added after a <pre> block. inline : collapses newline characters to a single space. <pre> keeps its Courier New font but no longer renders newlines. Each element must have a matching opening and closing tag; an unclosed tag (e.g. a <pre> with no </pre> ) produces invalid HTML.<br/>• [EE] Fixed :html heading rendering ( <h1> â <h6> ) in ODT templates: when a heading is not closed, the empty paragraph reproducing the browser's bottom spacing is now added. It was previously missing.
